<StatementSlide kicker="Workshop 3" source="In Workshop 2 you found what you can't walk back; in Workshop 3 you check what guards it">
  Audit Your Safety Net
</StatementSlide>

<TwoColumnSlide kicker="Workshop 3: your safety net" title="Your risk is what can reach main with nothing to stop it" divider wide>
  <div slot="left">
    <h3>How a change reaches main</h3>
    <ul class="reveal-list">
      <li>Who writes it: a teammate, an AI tool, or both</li>
      <li>Who reads it before it merges, if anyone</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div slot="right">
    <h3>What would stop a bad change</h3>
    <ul class="reveal-list">
      <li class="fragment">Tests on the paths that matter, that fail if they break</li>
      <li class="fragment">CI on every pull request, and green</li>
      <li class="fragment">Review on the hard-to-undo paths</li>
      <li class="fragment">A staging or preview environment</li>
      <li class="fragment">A rollback you've tried, not only planned</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <p class="caption">
    A rushed change from a teammate and an unread one from an AI tool slip
    through the same gaps. The more that merges unread, the more your checks
    have to catch.
  </p>
</TwoColumnSlide>

<Slide kicker="Workshop 3: the lunch app, audited" title="The lunch app, a few weeks in, check by check" wide>
  <SafetyNet checks={lunchChecks} stepped />
</Slide>

<Slide kicker="Workshop 3: the lunch app, audited" title="Start from its hardest decision: the data model" wide>
  <div class="gapfix">
    <div class="gap">
      <h3>The gap</h3>
      <p>
        Nothing stops a schema migration from merging without review, and it
        runs straight on the real database
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="fix fragment">
      <h3>The smallest change</h3>
      <p>
        Require a teammate's approval before any change to the migrations
        folder merges
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="caption">
    Close the gap at your hardest decision before you add tests to easy
    code.
  </p>
</Slide>

<Slide kicker="Workshop 3: name the gap" title="Name the change that slips through, not a general worry" wide>
  <div class="checks">
