        <li>We have no tests</li>
        <li>CI could be better</li>
        <li>We should review more</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="caption">
    A named gap says which bad change gets through and which check isn't there
    to stop it.
  </p>
</Slide>

<TwoColumnSlide kicker="Workshop 3 reference: two repositories" title="Tests that exist, and nothing that runs them" divider wide>
  <div slot="left">
    <h3>ephira, an inherited app</h3>
    <ul class="reveal-list">
      <li>The second team wrote four test files</li>
      <li>Its CI workflow ran only the linter, all year</li>
      <li><strong>Smallest change:</strong> one test step in the workflow</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="caption">
      A later commit added the tests to CI. Repository: <a href={ephira}>ephira on GitHub</a>
    </p>
  </div>
  <div slot="right">
    <h3>TaxonBodyMassML, a research project</h3>
    <ul class="reveal-list">
      <li class="fragment">Its test files sat beside the code, in each service's folder</li>
      <li class="fragment">CI ran pytest only if a <code>tests/</code> folder existed, and there wasn't one</li>
      <li class="fragment">So its test step printed "No tests implemented yet." and passed</li>
      <li class="fragment"><strong>Smallest change:</strong> point pytest at the test files, and fail when it finds none</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="caption">
      Repository: <a href={taxon}>TaxonBodyMassML on GitHub</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</TwoColumnSlide>

